THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
===================

rashomon is Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE). The released binaries are statically
linked and PURE GO -- CGO_ENABLED=0 -- so every third-party module would be
compiled INTO the artifact you download, and its licence would travel with it.

No third-party module is linked into ./cmd/rashomon on any platform the
release ships. The binary is the Go standard library and this repository's
own packages. The one dependency it carried, a pure-Go SQLite driver and the
libc translation beneath it, read a proxy's store that no longer exists in
this project; both went with it.

This file stays, because it is where the next dependency's notice is written
before its code ships. TestThirdPartyNotices_CoversEveryLinkedModule checks it
against `go list -deps ./cmd/rashomon` for every target the release builds,
and fails if a module is linked and not listed here at its version, or listed
here and not linked, or, once any module is linked, if this file carries no
licence text at all. The check finds licence text anywhere in the file, not
beside each module, so each module's licence is written here by whoever adds
the module. TestThirdPartyNotices_CheckerFailsClosed runs the same check
against dependency lists of its own.

